      "id": "CTN-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Counting all the conjugates of a cyclotomic layer",
      "anchor": "inputs-tower-norm",
      "statement": "For positive N and prime q coprime to N, the embedded cyclotomic fields K_N⊂K_qN admit a unique inclusion compatible with their maps to one algebraic closure. An automorphism fixing μ_N and acting as a generator on μ_q restricts to a generator of Gal(K_qN/K_N). Its q−1 powers in the norm operator give the ordinary relative field norm.",
      "hypotheses": "Both fields are cyclotomic over ℚ. On the ambient field τ fixes all Nth roots of unity and acts on qth roots by a generator of (ℤ/qℤ)×.",
